<title>SINGAPORE: Chuan Hup year net down 21.1 percent.</title>
<headline>Chuan Hup year net down 21.1 percent.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30, 1996</p>
<p>(in million Singapore dollars unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit				 6.99  vs     8.85</p>
<p>    Group shares (cents)		   3.02  vs     3.89</p>
<p>    Dividend   (percent)		   3.00  vs     2.00</p>
<p>    Turnover				  86.25  vs    80.04</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			   9.27  vs    10.25</p>
<p>    Investment income			0.33  vs     0.31</p>
<p>    Other/interest income		  6.66  vs     9.62</p>
<p>    Interest expense			 2.38  vs     2.49</p>
<p>    Depreciation			    21.06  vs    21.36</p>
<p>    Associates		  (loss)     5.03  vs     3.81  (gain)</p>
<p>    Tax					  1.45  vs     1.16</p>
<p>    Minorities				 0.83  vs     0.24</p>
<p>Note - Diversified marine company Chuan Holdings Ltd said its contract manufacturing associate PCI Ltd suffered a substantial loss from internal business rationalisation and weakness in the electronics industry.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
